# RYZON AI Backend

## Purpose
This file defines the server-side foundation required for secure accounts, daily plan quotas, AI job tracking, and subscription entitlements. This is a design contract, not a deployed backend.

## Security rules
- Derive account ID from a verified authentication token; never trust a client-supplied user ID or plan.
- Use server time and a documented timezone policy for daily quota windows.
- Enforce quota atomically in the database to prevent concurrent requests exceeding limits.
- Reserve quota when a generation job is accepted; charge only after successful completion.
- Release reservations after confirmed failure or cancellation under the retry policy.
- Grant Premium only from a verified store entitlement, never a client-side toggle.
- Keep provider keys on the server; never ship secrets in the app or repository.

## Proposed Free limits
| Feature | Daily limit |
| --- | ---: |
| Cartoon reels | 5 |
| Photo-to-cartoon | 5 |
| Stories | 3 |
| Background changes | 3 |
| Movie posters | 1 |

The product proposal also includes 10-second Free reels, up to 2 characters, 3 basic styles, 3 basic voices, Tamil/English/Hindi, basic subtitles, 30/60-second splitter, storyboard preview, basic editing, 720p export, and up to 5 projects. These are requirements only; enforcement is not active.

## Proposed API
All endpoints use HTTPS. Authenticated endpoints require a verified bearer token.

- GET /v1/me/usage — return the authenticated account's plan, quota window, remaining counts, and reservations. Server calculates the window.
- POST /v1/generations — authenticate, verify entitlement, validate input, atomically reserve quota, create a job, and return its ID.
- GET /v1/generations/{jobId} — return safe job status only to the owning account.
- POST /v1/generations/{jobId}/cancel — cancel an owned job and release reservation only after confirmed cancellation.
- POST /v1/store/google-play/verify — verify purchase token with Google Play before granting entitlement. Validate product, package, state, expiry, refund/revocation, and acknowledgement.

## Suggested data model
- accounts: internal account ID, auth provider subject, created timestamp, status.
- plan_entitlements: account ID, plan, source, store product ID, verified state, valid-from, valid-until.
- quota_windows: account ID, window start/end, timezone policy.
- quota_usage: account ID, feature key, window ID, successful count, reserved count.
- generation_jobs: job ID, account ID, feature key, status, reservation ID, timestamps, provider reference.
- quota_reservations: reservation ID, job ID, account ID, feature key, state, timestamps.
- audit_events: minimal security and entitlement changes; never store raw secrets.

Use database transactions, unique constraints for account/window/feature reservation operations, and idempotency keys for job creation and purchase verification.

## Required tests before launch
- Simultaneous requests at the final remaining quota slot.
- Failed, cancelled, retried, and duplicate generation requests.
- Client clock/timezone manipulation.
- Expired, refunded, revoked, pending, and duplicate store purchases.
- Cross-account job access attempts.
- Account deletion and data retention.

## Not implemented
No backend framework, database, authentication provider, AI provider, Google Play Billing integration, production secrets, deployment, or live API is configured. Choose these before implementing executable services.
